{"name":"Inspiration Peak","hex":"#4fa183","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"inspiration","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The drawing of air into the lungs, accomplished in mammals by elevation of the chest walls and flattening of the diaphragm, as part of the act of breathing.","A single inward breath (intake of air)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspiration"},{"term":"peak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A point; the sharp end or top of anything that terminates in a point; as, the peak, or front, of a cap.","The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To raise the point of (a gaff) closer to perpendicular.","To raise an oar out of the water, fitting the handle into a round slot or socket located at the bottom of the boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inspiration Peak","blocks":[{"text":"Inspiration Peak is a glacial feature of the Leaf Hills Moraines and of Otter Tail County in the U.S. State of Minnesota and is the second highest peak in Otter Tail County. It is 22 miles (35 km) northwest of Alexandria. The peak rises about 310 feet (94 m) above the surrounding plains, to an elevation of about 1,727 feet (526 m) above sea level. It is the central feature of Inspiration Peak State Wayside, a small recreation area maintained by the Minnesota Department of Natural Resources, which manages it from nearby Lake Carlos State Park. The wayside has a paved parking lot and a picnic area. The hike to the top is a short but strenuous walk up a well-worn trail from the parking lot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/View_from_top_of_Inspiration_Peak.jpg/330px-View_from_top_of_Inspiration_Peak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inspiration_Peak","wikidata":"Q6038549"},{"title":"Inspiration Peak (Washington)","blocks":[{"text":"Inspiration Peak is a 7,891-foot (2,405-metre) mountain summit located in the Picket Range within North Cascades National Park in the state of Washington. The peak lies 0.28 mi (0.45 km) east of Mount Degenhardt, and 0.47 mi (0.76 km) west of McMillan Spires. Terror Glacier remnants lie to the south of the peaks, and the McMillan Cirque glaciers hang on the north slopes. The first ascent of Inspiration Peak was made in 1940 by Fred Beckey and his brother Helmy via the West Ridge. Inspiration Peak can be seen from the North Cascades National Park Newhalem visitor center, weather permitting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Inspiration_Peak_in_the_Picket_Range_of_the_North_Cascades%2C_Washington_state.jpg/330px-Inspiration_Peak_in_the_Picket_Range_of_the_North_Cascades%2C_Washington_state.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inspiration_Peak_(Washington)","wikidata":"Q49038846"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg/500px-Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg/1280px-Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg/500px-Inspiration_Peak_Path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Start of path to summit through oak mixed forest","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInspiration_Peak_Path.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Terror%2C_Degenhardt%2C_Inspiration%2C_McMillan_Spire.jpg/120px-Terror%2C_Degenhardt%2C_Inspiration%2C_McMillan_Spire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont